The committed budgets are contract inputs, not measurements from a developer
workstation. `ledger-full.txt` and `ledger-minimal.txt` were generated by the
pinned Ubuntu 24.04 x86_64-linux-gnu measurement described by Sprint 57:
GCC 13.3.0 and GNU binutils 2.42. `make size-check` regenerates and
byte-compares both files; `make size-update` is the explicit rebaseline path.

The absolute gate measures `stat -c %s` of the stripped file produced by the
Linux `SHIPPING=1` profile: `-O2`, `-DNDEBUG`, function/data sections, linker
section garbage collection, no build id, and no unwind tables.  The last four
choices affect only the shipping profile; ordinary, sanitizer, and
`perf-symbols` builds retain their normal debugging and profiling metadata.
`GC_SECTIONS=0` exists only to measure and record the linker-GC delta. The
committed ledgers name that delta as `gc_saved_bytes`.

Sprint 57 amendment S57-A1 sets the achievable glibc hard bars at 2 MiB full
and initially 1.5 MiB minimal. Amendment S57-A5 raises only the musl
static-PIE minimal bar to 1,600 KiB after required Sprint 57.12 core work
moved its hosted measurement from 1,562,480 to 1,582,960 bytes without an optional
module. Amendment S57-A6 raises the musl full bar to 2,112 KiB after required
UI and mouse work moved it from 2,090,896 to 2,115,472 bytes. The same source
change moved the pinned glibc full binary by 24,576 bytes, chiefly in
`core.ui`, while that binary remains below its unchanged 2 MiB gate. The
S59-A7 empty-block-row safety fix adds 41 bytes of `core.edit` text in the
pinned glibc minimal build. Its on-disk file steps from 1,570,464 to
1,574,560 bytes, crossing the old 1,572,864-byte gate. The minimal cap alone
moves to the next 4 KiB boundary, 1,576,960 bytes; the full binary remains
2,066,120 bytes and every single-module profile remains inside its cap.
Amendment S57.26-A2 records the shell completion engine of Sprints
57.23-57.26 (a context lexer, command specs, --help learning, a fish oracle
and history suggestions). It adds 119,569 bytes of `core.ui` and grows every
glibc profile by 122,880-126,976 bytes, taking full to 2,193,096 and past the
2 MiB evidence floor, and every musl profile by 126,976. No optional module
grew. The hosted caps move to the next 16 KiB boundary (full 2,195,456,
minimal 1,703,936) and the musl caps to the next 64 KiB boundary (2,359,296
and 1,835,008), the S59-A6 rules; the ledgers above are that run's pinned
measurement. Amendment S57.32-A1 adds the prompt editing set and
cd-aware completion (Sprints 57.28 and 57.32): 18,140 bytes of `core.ui`,
1,429 of `core.edit`, 940 of `core.text`, 20,480-24,576 per glibc profile
(full 2,213,576, minimal 1,726,112). Hosted caps move to the next 16 KiB
boundary (full 2,228,224, minimal 1,736,704); musl caps are unchanged. Amendment
S57.29-A1 moves only the FUSS-only and LSP-only caps (1,900,544 and 1,867,776):
Sprint 57.29's 3,718 bytes stepped each file three 4 KiB pages. Amendment S57.30-A1
moves only AI-only and minimal (1,884,160 and 1,753,088) after Sprint 57.30's
10,229 bytes of prompt history; full remains 2,228,224. Amendment S57.31-A1 moves
full, FUSS-only, LSP-only and plugins-only (2,244,608, 1,916,928, 1,884,160,
1,851,392) after Sprint 57.31's 12,159 bytes. Amendment S57.31-A2 moves the musl
caps (2,424,832 and 1,900,544) after Sprints 57.28-57.31 grew musl-full to
2,361,232 and musl-minimal to 1,849,200. Amendment S57.27-A1 moves all six glibc
caps (full 2,260,992, minimal 1,769,472, LSP-only 1,900,544, AI-only 1,916,928,
FUSS-only 1,933,312, plugins-only 1,867,776) after Sprint 57.27's 13,468 bytes
of persistent shell session. The
former 1.5 MiB full / 900 KiB minimal planning values remain post-1.0
optimization ratchets. They are not alternate measurements and must not be
selected by a CI flag.

The four single-module values are the Sprint 57 contract caps. Their `why`
fields record the pinned GCC build's on-disk delta over minimal, rounded
upward to the next 10 KiB. A local developer build is not acceptable
provenance for an update.

`make size-check` also drives a clean PTY open for the shipping full and
minimal binaries. `scripts/size-memory.sh` reads the `rss checkpoint=paint`
rows and enforces a peak no greater than 1.6 times the byte size of
`100m-code`; the minimal build additionally enforces a 6 MiB empty-buffer
first-paint ceiling. `make size-musl` applies both gates to the static musl
binary. Missing or malformed checkpoints are harness errors, never passes.

Size gates do not authorize feature removal. Core Yew, its invariants, and
the required minimal-build feature matrix remain fixed inputs. When their
measured implementation floor conflicts with a planning number, the work
stops for an evidence-backed amendment or deferral; the measurement must not
be made green by gutting behavior, weakening stability, or changing what is
counted.
